Z||000000||MooCow||07-25-2000||11:10 PM||||Almost everytime I get into my Fiero I have to turn the car on but it won't start so I sit there for like 4 seconds with the battery on and then turn the key a little farther and then it fires right up.  Why does it to that??  I do have a radio deck in there and when it flips all the way over I can then fire the car up.  Sometimes though but not often the car will just fire right up with no wait but most of the time I wait for my deck to flip over then fire it up.<BR>My car again is a 86SE v6 4 speed with 130,750 on it.<P>                             Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bugsy||07-25-2000||11:39 PM||||So the car won't turn over or won't fire if you hit the starter right away? If the engine cranks but won't fire right away, I'd suspect maybe a bad diaphram in the fuel pump allowing the fuel to flow back. I'm guessing here, someone please correct me if I'm wrong <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin||||reg||1
